    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0311" n="1045" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1045"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr. Neill.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-08-27"><hi rendition="#italic">August 27,
                        1890</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 73.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Hicks’s No. 56, of
                    December 20, 1889, and 91, of February 21, last, both relating to the claim of
                    the Hydrographic Commission of the Amazon against the Government of Peru, you
                    are instructed to ask the foreign office whether the treasury department has
                    made any report to it in regard to the claim; and if not, to urge that action
                    may be taken. Mr. Hicks stated that the justice of the claim was admitted by the
                    officials of the foreign office.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
